The TJX Companies, Inc. (TJX) **beat** its Q4 FY 2025 pre-tax margin guidance by **60 basis points (bps)**.

According to the company's Q3 FY 2025 earnings report and subsequent guidance updates, TJX initially projected a Q4 FY 2025 pre-tax profit margin of **11.3%**. In its Q4 FY 2025 earnings release on February 26, 2025, the company reported an actual consolidated pre-tax profit margin of **11.9%**. The difference between the actual result (11.9%) and the guidance (11.3%) is 0.6 percentage points, which equates to a **60 bps beat**.

The strong performance was primarily driven by consolidated comparable store sales increasing 5%, which was well above the company's plan, and an increase in customer transactions.

FINAL ANSWER: TJX beat its Q4 FY 2025 pre-tax margin guidance by 60 BPS.

